# ============================================================
# .dockerignore — Sovereign Commander Console
# HARDENED (Wave 2 / A4).
#
# WHY THE "**/" FORMS:
#   Docker matches a bare pattern (e.g. "node_modules") against the
#   CONTEXT ROOT ONLY. It does NOT match nested paths. Per Docker's
#   own docs, "**/*.go" excludes at the root AND in every subdirectory
#   ("**" = zero or more path segments). The previous file relied
#   entirely on bare/root-anchored patterns, so ANY nested copy of a
#   secret, a .git dir, or a node_modules tree would have been swept
#   into the builder layer by "COPY . .".
#   => Every exclusion below now uses the RECURSIVE "**/" form, and the
#      bare root form is retained alongside it as defence in depth.
#
# ORDERING RULE (Docker semantics): LAST matching line wins.
#   Therefore "!.env.example" MUST stay BELOW the "**/.env.*" rules,
#   otherwise the documented example file would stay excluded.
# ============================================================

# --- Version control: repo history is a credential-leak vector ---
**/.git
**/.git/**
**/.svn
**/.hg
**/.bzr
# Defensive guard: verified 2026-10-02 that NO nested clone of this
# repository exists under the context root, so this is currently a
# no-op. Kept deliberately so a nested checkout can never be swept in.
**/sovereign-commander-console

# --- Secrets: must never enter the build context ---
# Runtime secrets are supplied to the CONTAINER as ENV via "docker run
# -e ..." (confirmed in docker inspect), not read from the context.
# Excluding these is build-safe: the app has ZERO import.meta.env and
# ZERO VITE_* usage, so Vite inlines nothing from .env at build time;
# all secret reads are process.env at RUNTIME.
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Catch-all for arbitrarily-named env files at any depth (e.g. a
# nested "local.env"); none exist in this repo today, and no required
# build input ends in ".env", so this cannot break the build.
**/*.env
!.env.example
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/.netrc
**/credentials
**/*credential*
**/secrets.env
# Host MCP tree (E:\Servers-Center) uses an "env/secrets.env" layout;
# blocked here so that tree can never be copied in if ever mounted in.
**/env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa
**/id_rsa.*
**/id_ed25519*

# --- Dependencies / build output: both rebuilt inside the image ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite
**/coverage

# --- Logs (pre-existing rules, now recursive) ---
*.log
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
**/npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Package-manager / bundler caches ---
**/.yarn
**/.pnpm-store
**/.cache
**/.turbo
**/.parcel-cache

# --- Editor / OS / agent tooling noise ---
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.agents
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini

# --- Docker build plumbing ---
# Safe to ignore: Docker still transmits the Dockerfile and the
# .dockerignore itself to the builder regardless of these rules, because
# the builder needs them. They are excluded only so that "COPY . ."
# does not bake them into an image layer.
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
**/Dockerfile.*
docker-compose*
**/docker-compose*
.dockerignore
**/.dockerignore

# --- CI/CD + deploy automation: must not be baked into layers ---
**/.github
cloudbuild.yaml
deploy-to-gcp.sh

# --- Local scratch / screenshot output ---
# (pre-existing exclusions, retained and made recursive)
scratch
**/scratch
screenshots
**/screenshots

# ============================================================
# DELIBERATELY KEPT IN THE CONTEXT (required by the build):
#   package.json, package-lock.json   -> "npm ci" in BOTH stages
#                                      (COPY package*.json)
#   tsconfig.json                     -> read by esbuild/tsx + tsc
#   vite.config.ts                    -> vite build config
#   index.html                        -> vite entry HTML
#   src/**                            -> browser bundle + server.ts
#                                      imports (./src/os/kernelEngine,
#                                      ./src/services/*, ./src/workspace/*)
#   public/**                         -> copied to runner as ./public
#   server.ts                         -> esbuild bundles -> dist/server.cjs
#   firebase-applet-config.json       -> src/firebase.ts imports
#                                      '../firebase-applet-config.json'
#   opencode.json                     -> runtime MCP/host topology config
#   config/**, scripts/**, docs/**    -> not build inputs; kept to avoid
#                                      breaking runtime/tooling paths.
# ============================================================